fix(routes): mint ruby/php/elixir/swift route markers via the chokepoint (WI-zugob)

Producer batch 1 of the route-marker fleet sweep, scoped deliberately to the
producers whose migration does NOT change node.name.

All four already set Symbol.name to "{METHOD} {path}" -- the exact string
make_route_symbol mints -- so the only output change is the node.id KIND-SLOT:
the ADR-0027 Phase-3 fossil where the id carried the literal `route` while
Symbol.kind was already `function` (and `route` is not a registered symbol kind,
so id_format flagged every one). Measured before/after on the route-parity
fixtures: names byte-identical, ids `...:GET /users:route` -> `...:GET /users:function`.

  ruby   3 sites (Rails resources / resource / plain-verb)
  php    2 sites (Laravel resource + single-verb)
  elixir 2 sites (Phoenix resources + single/LiveView)
  swift  1 site  (Vapor)

Also fixes elixir's EMPTY Symbol.origin. The cause was not in the route code:
TreeSitterAnalyzer.pass_id defaults to "" and the effective id is resolved
downstream as `self.pass_id or make_pass_id(self.lang)`, so elixir threading
self.pass_id into its route extractor stamped the empty string -- while every
other elixir symbol got the right id from the fallback. The route path was the
one place bypassing the resolution. Now passes the module PASS_ID, with the
reason recorded at the call site so it does not get "tidied" back.

Swift needed an explicit leading slash to stay name-preserving: Vapor route
components arrive without one and the old producer built its name as
f"{http_method} /{route_path}", while the factory normalizes only the EMPTY path
to "/". Passing the raw component would have silently renamed GET /users to
GET users. Noted at the call site.

Ratchet: 67 passed / 16 xfailed -> 72 passed / 11 xfailed (4 kind-slot holes +
the origin hole drained).

